      "source": [
        "# Digital Design - mod-13\n\n",
        "**Course:** digital-design\n\n",
        "Run the code cells below to practice.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Inputs \u2192 [AND Array] \u2192 [OR Array] \u2192 Outputs\n\nThe AND array generates product terms (minterms or partial products)\nThe OR array combines product terms into sum-of-products outputs"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Example: 3-input, 4-product-term, 2-output PLA\n\nInputs: A, B, C (and their complements A', B', C')\n\nAND array (programmable connections):\n  P1 = A\u00b7B'      (connect A and B' to AND gate 1)\n  P2 = B\u00b7C       (connect B and C to AND gate 2)\n  P3 = A\u00b7C'      (connect A and C' to AND gate 3)\n  P4 = A'\u00b7B\u00b7C'   (connect A', B, C' to AND gate 4)\n\nOR array (programmable connections):\n  F1 = P1 + P2   (connect product terms 1,2 to OR gate 1)\n  F2 = P3 + P4   (connect product terms 3,4 to OR gate 2)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Example: PAL with 3 inputs, each output has 3 dedicated product terms\n\n  F1 = P1 + P2 + P3        (OR of its 3 dedicated AND gates)\n  F2 = P4 + P5 + P6        (OR of its 3 dedicated AND gates)\n\n  P1 through P3 can be programmed to any product term\n  P4 through P6 can be programmed to any product term\n  But F1 can only use P1-P3; F2 can only use P4-P6"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "n-input ROM:\n- Fixed AND array: 2^n AND gates (full decoder, all minterms)\n- Programmable OR array: each output selects which minterms to include\n\nAny function of n variables can be implemented without simplification!"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Intact fuse:     \u2500\u2500X\u2500\u2500  (connected)\nBlown fuse:      \u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500  (disconnected)\nHardwired:       \u2500\u2500\u25cf\u2500\u2500  (permanent connection)\n\nBefore programming: all fuses intact (all connections made)\nProgramming: selectively blow fuses to remove unwanted connections"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Product terms needed: A'B', AC', B'C, AB\n  P1 = A'B'  \u2192 used by F1\n  P2 = AC'   \u2192 used by F1\n  P3 = B'C   \u2192 used by F2\n  P4 = AB    \u2192 used by F2\n\nOR connections:\n  F1 = P1 + P2\n  F2 = P3 + P4"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Evolution timeline:\nPLA (1970s) \u2192 PAL (1978) \u2192 CPLD (1980s) \u2192 FPGA (1985-present)\n\nComplexity:\nPLA: ~100 gates | PAL: ~500 gates | CPLD: ~10K gates | FPGA: ~1M+ gates"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "verilog",
          "// This Verilog synthesizes efficiently to PLD architecture\nmodule pld_functions(\n    input  wire A, B, C,\n    output wire F1, F2\n);\n    // SOP form maps directly to PLD AND-OR structure\n    assign F1 = (~A & ~B) | (A & ~C);\n    assign F2 = (~B & C) | (A & B);\nendmodule"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "verilog",
          "// PAL-style registered output (with flip-flop)\nmodule pal_registered(\n    input  wire       clk,\n    input  wire [2:0] inputs,\n    output reg  [1:0] outputs\n);\n    always @(posedge clk) begin\n        outputs[0] <= (~inputs[2] & ~inputs[1]) | (inputs[2] & ~inputs[0]);\n        outputs[1] <= (~inputs[1] & inputs[0]) | (inputs[2] & inputs[1]);\n    end\nendmodule"
        ]
      ]
    }
